#!/usr/bin/env bun
// Voice prebuild: counts the texts in villagers, packs, modules, scenarios, the school's course (what the teacher reads
// of each unit's introduction: its examples, quick questions and their answers, the Slovene of its explanations; the
// explanations themselves in the learner's own language apart, --explanations), scenes, the cast's arrivals, «Vidim, vidim» (what a child says
// playing I spy in the scenes: companion/ispy), the keepers' talks (the culture's spots: the charcoal burner's meeting and
// his story), the village projects' steps (the culture's project-steps/) and its ages' parties (celebrations/), the storyteller's
// stories and the car's drills (Slovene, or the
// language of the learner's culture pack, LANI_CULTURE, with its own voice cast), what is voiced, what is missing and
// the ElevenLabs quota left. With --run, generates the missing clips in priority order (villager lines in their
// speakers' voices, pack words, examples, modules, scenarios, the stories' tellings at A1, the drills at A1, scenes,
// the keepers' talks and the projects' steps, I spy's lines (in the voice of each child who may play there), the
// learner's own lines (the dialogs' choices) in their own voice (my-voice.ts; none while their lines are off), then the tellings at A2, the drills
// above A1, the tellings at B1 and up; a telling and a
// riddle in the teller's voice, their own designed one where it is ready ("@janez": ElevenLabs only), a drill's other
// texts in the narrator's: the car plays a story or a drill's item only when its clips exist):
// ElevenLabs down to the reserve, then the local worker (not for a villager line whose narrator clip
// exists: the app plays that one until ElevenLabs makes theirs).
//
// In a Slovene village the narrators (female, male) speak with their native Slovene ElevenLabs voices (Nina, Luka: the
// cast's "languages" "sl"), the local Gepard voice as their fallback (female: ana for a lone word, nina for a sentence;
// male: marko), never the English library voices (README, "Voice"; LANI_VOICE_NARRATOR_SL=gepard: the local voice first).
// --run makes a narrator line's clip in its Slovene ElevenLabs voice in the priority order, within the budget, also where
// its local clip is there (which stays, as the fallback). Elsewhere an English narrator says a short text (1–3 words)
// inside a carrier sentence, which is cut out, and the plan shows how many narrator words are still old-style (said
// plainly) and what re-voicing them costs.
//
// Usage: companion/bin/voice-build [--run] [--upgrade] [--revoice speaker[,speaker]] [--only voice[,voice]] [--explanations] [--base xx[,yy]] [--max-chars N] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --revoice-words [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --denoise [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --level [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --edges [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --pace [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]   (also --tempo)
//        companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard SNAPSHOT [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --narrators [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --upgrade-model [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//   --upgrade        also replace local (Gepard) clips with ElevenLabs ones while the quota lasts
//   --revoice S      make every clip of speaker S again with ElevenLabs (after swapping its voice in companion/voice-cast.json)
//   --max-chars N    spend at most N ElevenLabs characters in this run
//   --only V         plan and make only the texts of these voices (speaker[,speaker]: --only teacher, Učiteljica Mojca's
//                    lines, her course, her arrival; someone's own voice counts as their speaker's, and "@mojca" names it)
//   --explanations   also the course's explanations in the learner's own language (one clip a step and a summary: the
//                    teacher's lines in English with the Slovene forms inside: ~29,000 characters for the 18 units and
//                    their summaries), made by ElevenLabs only; without it the plan counts them apart and what they would
//                    cost (the app asks for them as an intro opens)
//   --base xx[,yy]   the learner's own languages the course's explanations and their runs are read in (en, de, it);
//                    default: the learner profile's base_language
//   --revoice-words  only the old-style short narrator words again, in their carrier sentence, most asked for first,
//                    at most --max N of them, within the reserve (the bridge does this lazily, a few a day)
//   --denoise        the clips of the voices the cast marks "denoise" (a voice that hisses) through their filter, those
//                    not filtered yet (the bridge filters new ones as it stores them), at most --max N; each under a new
//                    file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded. Levelled in the same encode.
//   --level          every clip not at the level yet (one loudness, LEVEL in bridge/src/voice.ts: −18 LUFS, true peak
//                    at most −1.5 dBTP; the bridge levels new clips as it stores them), oldest first, at most --max N.
//                    The dry run measures them and shows each voice's loudness before and the gain. A clip is levelled
//                    once: its row records the target (level) and the gain; after a change of the target, --level
//                    levels the clips again from their files as they are (one more encode; a clip within 0.5 dB of the
//                    target keeps its file). A clip whose voice's filter is due is filtered in the same encode. Each
//                    under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded; a running bridge tells
//                    the app within a minute (voice_updated).
//   --edges          every clip whose silence at the edges isn't trimmed yet (EDGES in bridge/src/voice.ts: 0.05 s kept
//                    before the sound, 0.1 s after it; the bridge trims new clips as it stores them), of every engine,
//                    oldest first, at most --max N. The dry run measures them: per engine, how many have more than
//                    0.1 s of silence before the sound or 0.2 s after it (twice what is kept), and the silence now and
//                    after. --run trims those, levelled again in the same encode, each under a new file name, the old
//                    file removed once the new one is recorded; the others are only recorded (edges), so no clip is
//                    done twice.
//   --pace           (also --tempo) the clips not at their pace yet, at most --max N: a voice's own (the cast's "tempo"
//                    on a speaker: a voice that speaks slowly, its clips sped up, the pitch kept; a number for every
//                    engine, or by engine: "tempo": { "elevenlabs": 1.1 }, the girl's Piku), and the local (Gepard)
//                    clips at the local voice's pace when one is set (LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_TEMPO, a factor;
//                    LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_PAUSES, the longest pause kept; neither by default: the local voice keeps its
//                    own pace). Each clip records the factor it is at (tempo), so it is paced once; a voice's tempo
//                    changed, its clips are paced by the difference (back to 1: slowed down again). The dry run
//                    measures each clip's characters a second now and as it would be paced, per voice. Levelled again
//                    in the same encode, under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded.
//                    --denoise, --level, --edges and --pace use ffmpeg only: no ElevenLabs, no characters.
//   --restore-gepard SNAPSHOT
//                    the local clips paced before (tempo set: October 2026's ×1.05 pass) back to their files and rows in
//                    SNAPSHOT, a lani-backup snapshot taken before that (its voice/, or a voice store's directory: voice.db
//                    and files/; read only, its database from a copy). The dry run lists what it would restore and what
//                    it can't; --run copies each file back (checked byte for byte), points the row at it with the
//                    snapshot's level and gain, and removes the paced file once the row is moved. Then --edges trims them.
//   --narrators      in a Slovene village: the narrators' local clips (female, male) not in their local voice yet
//                    (female: ana for a lone word, nina for a sentence; male: marko; ElevenLabs' English narrators from
//                    before) made again by the local worker, most asked for first, at most --max N, one at a time
//                    (about a second each). Only Slovene texts: a clip of this village's corpus, of a source the corpus
//                    has (a pack, a scene, …), or a line the app spoke here (live, road); the dry run lists the others,
//                    which stay as they are. The edges trimmed and levelled as every new clip; a worker that is down
//                    stops the run, and the next run goes on. The narrators' clips in their Slovene ElevenLabs voices
//                    are left as they are (rows of their own); no ElevenLabs.
//   --upgrade-model  the ElevenLabs clips made with an older model than LANI_ELEVENLABS_MODEL (eleven_v4_turbo by default;
//                    a clip from before the model was recorded: eleven_v3) made again in it, most played first (hits),
//                    within the quota above the reserve, at most --max N clips and --max-chars N characters. Each in its
//                    voice (a short word in its carrier sentence, an explanation plainly), its filter, edges and level as
//                    every new clip, under a new file name, the old file removed; a running bridge tells the app within a
//                    minute (voice_updated). Never a local (Gepard) clip, nor the family's recordings. The dry run lists the
//                    clips per model, what would be made and what it costs.
//   --elevenlabs S   speaker S's local (Gepard) clips, made while ElevenLabs couldn't (the quota, an error), made again in
//                    S's ElevenLabs voice, most played first, within the quota above the reserve, at most --max N clips
//                    and --max-chars N characters; filtered, trimmed and levelled as every new clip, under a new file
//                    name, the local file removed; a running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated). Never
//                    the narrators (female, male: their local clips stay beside their Slovene ElevenLabs ones). E.g.
//                    --elevenlabs teacher: Učiteljica Mojca's lines the local voice said for her (Jan, 2026-10-16).
//                    Drama 3's clips count as local here too: ElevenLabs ranks above Drama 3, Drama 3 above Gepard.
//   --drama3 S       speaker S's local Gepard clips (S: speaker[,speaker], or all: every speaker but the narrators) made
//                    again by the local Drama 3 worker (companion/voice-drama3; Built with Fish Audio), most played first,
//                    at most --max N; each take passes the worker's checks (the gender by pitch, noise, the text heard
//                    by Whisper, length and silence) or is made again with another seed; a line no take passes is
//                    reported and keeps its Gepard clip (tried again only with --retry-failed). Trimmed and levelled as
//                    every new clip, under a new file name, the Gepard file removed; a running bridge tells the app within
//                    a minute (voice_updated). The dry run shows the clips, an estimate of the time at the measured speed
//                    (LANI_DRAMA3_RTF) and the worker. --run starts the worker (LANI_DRAMA3_CMD, else
//                    ~/.local/share/lani-drama3/run.sh) unless one answers at LANI_DRAMA3_URL (127.0.0.1:8785), and stops
//                    it after; the worker holds the host's heavy lock (LANI_HEAVY_LOCK, /tmp/lani-heavy.lock) while it
//                    runs; the batch pauses below 20 GB available (LANI_DRAMA3_MIN_FREE_GB) and goes on when memory is
//                    back. Stopped (Ctrl-C), it goes on where it stopped with the next --run. Never the narrators.
//   --data DIR       the learner data directory, as LANI_DATA_DIR (a copy; another learner's profiles/<id>/data with
//                    their LANI_CULTURE)
// Without --run, a dry run. The key comes from ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, else ~/.config/lani/keys.env (LANI_KEYS_FILE).
import '../bridge/src/env' // first: LANI_* from the FLUENT_* names of a node set up before the rename
import { existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs'
import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path'
import { addresseeOf } from '../bridge/src/addressee'
import { ArrivalStore, cultureArrivals } from '../bridge/src/arrivals'
import { cast, castVoiced, denoiseVoices, isSpeaker, PERSON_VOICE, personVoice, tempoVoices, useCastFile, usePersonVoices } from '../bridge/src/cast'
import { CourseStore, courseDir } from '../bridge/src/course'
import { familyHas, indexHas } from '../bridge/src/course-speech'
import { childOf, learnerLangs } from '../bridge/src/learners'
import { mineVoice } from '../bridge/src/my-voice'
import { ownVoicesIn } from '../bridge/src/profiles'
import { cultureDir, cultureKeepers, keeperTellings, resolveCulture } from '../bridge/src/cultures'
import { cultureStepFiles, stepTellings } from '../bridge/src/project-steps'
import { cultureCelebrationFiles, partyTellings } from '../bridge/src/celebrations'
import { DrillStore, drillsDir } from '../bridge/src/drills'
import { grammarDir, GrammarStore } from '../bridge/src/grammar'
import { readISpy } from '../bridge/src/ispy'
import { ModuleStore } from '../bridge/src/store'
import { PackStore, packsDirs } from '../bridge/src/packs'
import { ScenarioStore } from '../bridge/src/scenarios'
import { SceneStore, scenesDirs } from '../bridge/src/scenes'
import { StoryStore, storiesDirs } from '../bridge/src/stories'
import { VillagerStore } from '../bridge/src/villagers'
import { cardTexts, charsPerSecond, clipKey, corpus, creditsFor, Drama3, lazyModelUpgrade, EDGES, explanationLang, modelOf, enginesFromEnv, ffmpegDenoiser, ffmpegFileEdges, ffmpegLeveller, ffmpegLoudness, ffmpegPace, FILE, LEVEL, levelGain, LIMIT_MARGIN, paceChain, redoDaily, revoiceDaily, sloveneNarrators, trimmable, VoiceStore, type Clip, type Edges, type Loudness, type Pace } from '../bridge/src/voice'
import { formatPlan, plan, run } from '../bridge/src/prebuild'
import { availableGb, drama3Estimate, drama3Settings, Drama3Worker, duration, memoryGate } from '../bridge/src/drama3'
import { normalizeText } from '../bridge/src/family'
import { keysFile } from '../bridge/src/env'
import { voiceDir } from '../bridge/src/paths'
import { setting } from '../bridge/src/env'

const root = resolve(import.meta.dir, '../..')
// the learner's village's culture pack (LANI_CULTURE, as their bridge has it; primorska by default): its language,
// its cast, its voice cast, its packs and its own scenes
const cultures = process.env.LANI_CULTURES_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/cultures')
// (lani.env's for the default learner; another --data directory's comes from LANI_CULTURE in the environment only)
const dataArg = process.argv.indexOf('--data') >= 0 ? process.argv[process.argv.indexOf('--data') + 1] : undefined
const village = resolveCulture(cultures, setting('LANI_CULTURE', dataArg ? { ...process.env, LANI_DATA_DIR: resolve(dataArg) } : process.env))
const culture = village.id
const language = village.manifest?.language ?? 'sl'
// the curated content of the village's language (a subdirectory for another than Slovene, as the bridge has it)
const ofLanguage = (dir: string) => (language === 'sl' ? dir : join(dir, language))
const castFile = join(cultureDir(cultures, culture), 'voice-cast.json')
if (existsSync(castFile)) useCastFile(castFile)

const args = process.argv.slice(2)
const flag = (f: string) => args.includes(f)
const maxAt = args.indexOf('--max-chars')
const maxChars = maxAt >= 0 ? Number(args[maxAt + 1]) : undefined
const revAt = args.indexOf('--revoice')
const revoice = revAt >= 0 ? (args[revAt + 1] ?? '').split(',').filter(Boolean) : []
const unknown = revoice.filter(s => !isSpeaker(s))
const revoiceWords = flag('--revoice-words')
const denoise = flag('--denoise')
const level = flag('--level')
// --pace (also --tempo, its name before the voices' own tempo): the clips not at their pace yet
const tempo = flag('--tempo') || flag('--pace')
const paceFlag = flag('--pace') ? '--pace' : '--tempo'
const edges = flag('--edges')
const narrators = flag('--narrators')
const upgradeModel = flag('--upgrade-model')
const elAt = args.indexOf('--elevenlabs')
const elevenSpeakers = elAt >= 0 ? (args[elAt + 1] ?? '').split(',').filter(Boolean) : []
const elevenUnknown = elevenSpeakers.filter(s => !isSpeaker(s))
const elevenNarrators = elevenSpeakers.filter(s => s === 'female' || s === 'male')
const toEleven = elAt >= 0
const d3At = args.indexOf('--drama3')
const d3Arg = d3At >= 0 ? (args[d3At + 1] ?? '') : ''
const toDrama3 = d3At >= 0
// all: every speaker of the village's cast but the narrators
const d3Speakers = d3Arg === 'all' ? Object.keys(cast()).filter(s => s !== 'female' && s !== 'male') : d3Arg.split(',').filter(Boolean)
const d3Unknown = d3Speakers.filter(s => !isSpeaker(s))
const d3Narrators = d3Speakers.filter(s => s === 'female' || s === 'male')
const restoreAt = args.indexOf('--restore-gepard')
const snapshotArg = restoreAt >= 0 ? args[restoreAt + 1] : undefined
// a lani-backup snapshot (its voice/), or a voice store's own directory (voice.db and files/)
const snapshot = snapshotArg ? [join(snapshotArg, 'voice'), snapshotArg].find(d => existsSync(join(d, 'voice.db')) && existsSync(join(d, 'files'))) : undefined
const badSnapshot = restoreAt >= 0 && !snapshot
const restore = restoreAt >= 0
const maxAt2 = args.indexOf('--max')
const max = maxAt2 >= 0 ? Number(args[maxAt2 + 1]) : undefined
const badMax = max !== undefined && !(Number.isInteger(max) && max >= 0)
const dataAt = args.indexOf('--data')
const data = dataAt >= 0 ? args[dataAt + 1] : undefined
const badData = dataAt >= 0 && !(data && existsSync(data) && statSync(data).isDirectory())
// --only: the texts of these voices only (a speaker of the cast, or someone's own voice "@mojca", checked once the voice
// profiles are read)
const onlyAt = args.indexOf('--only')
const only = onlyAt >= 0 ? (args[onlyAt + 1] ?? '').split(',').filter(Boolean) : []
const onlyUnknown = only.filter(s => !isSpeaker(s) && !PERSON_VOICE.test(s))
const explanations = flag('--explanations')
const baseAt = args.indexOf('--base')
const bases = baseAt >= 0 ? (args[baseAt + 1] ?? '').split(',').filter(Boolean) : []
const badBase = baseAt >= 0 && (!bases.length || bases.some(b => !/^[a-z]{2}$/.test(b) || b === language))
const modes = [revoiceWords, denoise, level, tempo, edges, restore, narrators, upgradeModel, toEleven, toDrama3, revAt >= 0 || flag('--upgrade')].filter(Boolean).length
const ffmpegOnly = denoise || level || tempo || edges || restore || narrators
// --only, --explanations and --base shape the corpus's plan and run: not another mode's
const corpusFlags = onlyAt >= 0 || explanations || baseAt >= 0
const otherMode = revoiceWords || denoise || level || tempo || edges || restore || narrators || upgradeModel || toEleven || toDrama3
if (flag('--help') || flag('-h') || (onlyAt >= 0 && (!only.length || onlyUnknown.length)) || badBase || (corpusFlags && otherMode) || (maxChars !== undefined && !(maxChars >= 0)) || (revAt >= 0 && !revoice.length) || unknown.length || badMax || badData || badSnapshot || (maxAt2 >= 0 && !revoiceWords && !upgradeModel && !toEleven && !toDrama3 && !ffmpegOnly) || modes > 1 || (ffmpegOnly && maxAt >= 0) || (toEleven && (!elevenSpeakers.length || elevenUnknown.length || elevenNarrators.length)) || (toDrama3 && (!d3Speakers.length || d3Unknown.length || d3Narrators.length || maxAt >= 0)) || (flag('--retry-failed') && !toDrama3)) {
  if (unknown.length) console.error(`not in the voice cast: ${unknown.join(', ')} (the cast: ${Object.keys(cast()).join(', ')})`)
  if (elevenUnknown.length) console.error(`--elevenlabs: not in the voice cast: ${elevenUnknown.join(', ')} (the cast: ${Object.keys(cast()).join(', ')})`)
  if (elevenNarrators.length) console.error(`--elevenlabs: not the narrators (${elevenNarrators.join(', ')}): their local clips stay beside their Slovene ElevenLabs ones (--narrators)`)
  if (d3Unknown.length) console.error(`--drama3: not in the voice cast: ${d3Unknown.join(', ')} (the cast: ${Object.keys(cast()).join(', ')}, or all)`)
  if (d3Narrators.length) console.error(`--drama3: not the narrators (${d3Narrators.join(', ')}): their local voices stay Gepard's, the fallback of their Slovene ElevenLabs voices`)
  if (toDrama3 && !d3Speakers.length) console.error('--drama3: which speakers? speaker[,speaker] or all')
  if (badData) console.error(`--data: no directory ${data ?? ''}`)
  if (onlyAt >= 0 && !only.length) console.error('--only: which voices? speaker[,speaker] (--only teacher)')
  if (onlyUnknown.length) console.error(`--only: not in the voice cast: ${onlyUnknown.join(', ')} (the cast: ${Object.keys(cast()).join(', ')}, or someone's own voice: @mojca)`)
  if (badBase) console.error(`--base: the learner's own languages, two letters each, not the village's (${language}): en, de, it`)
  if (corpusFlags && otherMode) console.error('--only, --explanations and --base go with the plan and --run (--upgrade, --revoice), not another mode')
  if (badSnapshot) console.error(`--restore-gepard: no voice store (voice.db and files/) in ${snapshotArg ?? '(none given)'} or its voice/`)
  console.log('Usage: companion/bin/voice-build [--run] [--upgrade] [--revoice speaker[,speaker]] [--only voice[,voice]] [--explanations] [--base xx[,yy]] [--max-chars N] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --revoice-words [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --denoise [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --level [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --edges [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --pace [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]   (also --tempo)')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard SNAPSHOT [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --narrators [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --upgrade-model [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --elevenlabs speaker[,speaker] [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --drama3 speaker[,speaker]|all [--max N] [--retry-failed] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  process.exit(flag('--help') || flag('-h') ? 0 : 2)
}
// the data directory the clips are in (ensure_data_dir.py reads LANI_DATA_DIR)
if (data) process.env.LANI_DATA_DIR = resolve(data)

// The key file holds KEY=value lines; only what isn't already in the environment is taken.
const keys = keysFile()
if (existsSync(keys)) {
  for (const line of readFileSync(keys, 'utf8').split('\n')) {
    const m = /^\s*(?:export\s+)?([A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*)\s*=\s*(.*?)\s*$/.exec(line)
    if (m && process.env[m[1]] === undefined) process.env[m[1]] = m[2].replace(/^(['"])(.*)\1$/, '$2')
  }
}

const p = Bun.spawnSync(['python3', '.claude/hooks/ensure_data_dir.py'], { cwd: root, env: { ...process.env, CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR: root } })
if (p.exitCode !== 0) throw new Error(`ensure_data_dir.py failed: ${p.stderr.toString()}`)
const appDir = join(p.stdout.toString().trim(), 'app')
// the clips: the voice cache ($LANI_VOICE_CACHE, lani.env's for the default learner), else <data>/app/voice

const log = (...a: unknown[]) => console.error('[voice-build]', ...a)
// the store as the bridge has it: the narrators of a Slovene village in their Slovene ElevenLabs voices, the local voice as
// their fallback (LANI_VOICE_NARRATOR_SL), the day's re-voice cap and re-records (LANI_VOICE_REVOICE_DAILY,
// LANI_VOICE_REDO_DAILY: lani.env's or keys.env's)
const villageVoices = { language, narrators: sloveneNarrators(language, process.env, log), revoiceDaily: revoiceDaily(process.env), redoDaily: redoDaily(process.env), lazyModel: lazyModelUpgrade(process.env) }

if (denoise) {
  // the clips of the voices that hiss, through their filter: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const voices = denoiseVoices()
  const queue = store.denoiseQueue()
  const summary = { voices, waiting: queue.length, stats: store.denoiseStats(), dir: store.dir }
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, clips: queue.slice(0, max).map(c => ({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, file: c.file, preset: c.preset, text: c.text })) }, null, 2))
    else {
      console.log(`Voices filtered (the cast's "denoise"): ${Object.entries(voices).map(([v, p]) => `${v} (${p})`).join(', ') || 'none'}`)
      console.log(`Clips in ${store.dir} waiting for their filter: ${queue.length}${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
      for (const c of queue.slice(0, max)) console.log(`  ${c.preset.padEnd(11)} ${c.voice.padEnd(10)} ${c.file}  ${c.text.length > 64 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 63)}…` : c.text}`)
      console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each would be filtered with ffmpeg${summary.stats.ffmpeg ? '' : ' (not found here: LANI_FFMPEG)'} and brought to the level in the same encode, and stored under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded.`)
      console.log(`Filter with: companion/bin/voice-build --denoise --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    }
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegDenoiser()) {
    console.error('voice-build --denoise: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Filtering ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s) …`)
  const r = await store.denoiseClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nFiltered ${r.done} clip(s)${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (level) {
  // every clip at one loudness: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const queue = store.levelQueue()
  const target = store.levelTarget
  const tail = `${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    // each clip measured as it would be levelled (through its voice's filter and a local clip's pace when they are due):
    // nothing is written
    const measure = ffmpegLoudness()
    const voices = denoiseVoices()
    const list = queue.slice(0, max)
    if (!measure) console.error('voice-build --level: no ffmpeg here (LANI_FFMPEG names one): nothing measured')
    else if (list.length) console.error(`Measuring ${list.length} clip(s) …`)
    type Row = { key: string; voice: string; engine: string; file: string; text: string; denoise?: string; tempo?: number; before?: Loudness; gain?: number; limit?: boolean; keep?: boolean }
    const rows: Row[] = []
    let next = 0
    await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 4 }, async () => {
      while (next < list.length) {
        const c = list[next++]
        const path = join(store.filesDir, c.file)
        const pre = c.engine === 'elevenlabs' && !c.denoise ? voices[c.voice] : undefined
        const pace = store.paceDue(c)
        const m = measure && FILE.test(c.file) && existsSync(path) ? await measure(new Uint8Array(readFileSync(path)), { denoise: pre, pace }) : null
        const g = m ? levelGain(m, { ...LEVEL, target }) : undefined
        rows.push({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, engine: c.engine, file: c.file, text: c.text, ...(pre ? { denoise: pre } : {}), ...(pace ? { tempo: pace.tempo } : {}), ...(m && g ? { before: m, gain: g.gain, limit: g.limit, keep: g.keep && !pre && !pace } : {}) })
      }
    }))
    const q = (xs: number[], f: number) => {
      const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b)
      return s.length ? s[Math.min(s.length - 1, Math.floor(f * (s.length - 1) + 0.5))] : NaN
    }
    const by = new Map<string, Row[]>()
    for (const r of rows) by.set(`${r.voice} ${r.engine}`, [...(by.get(`${r.voice} ${r.engine}`) ?? []), r])
    const groups = [...by].map(([name, g]) => {
      const m = g.filter(r => r.before && r.before.lufs > -70)
      const lufs = m.map(r => r.before!.lufs)
      const gains = m.map(r => r.gain!)
      // how far over the limiter's threshold the gain alone would take the limited clips' true peaks: what it holds back
      const limited = m.filter(r => r.limit && !r.keep)
      return {
        name, clips: g.length, measured: m.length,
        lufs: { median: q(lufs, 0.5), p10: q(lufs, 0.1), p90: q(lufs, 0.9) },
        gain: { median: q(gains, 0.5), min: Math.min(...gains), max: Math.max(...gains) },
        kept: g.filter(r => r.keep).length, limited: limited.length, over: q(limited.map(r => r.before!.peak + r.gain! - (LEVEL.peak - LIMIT_MARGIN)), 0.5), denoise: g.filter(r => r.denoise).length, paced: g.filter(r => r.tempo).length,
      }
    }).sort((a, b) => b.lufs.median - a.lufs.median)
    const summary = { target, peak: LEVEL.peak, waiting: queue.length, measured: rows.filter(r => r.before).length, ffmpeg: !!measure, dir: store.dir }
    if (flag('--json')) {
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, voices: Object.fromEntries(groups.map(({ name, ...g }) => [name, g])), clips: rows }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    const f1 = (x: number) => (Number.isFinite(x) ? `${x > 0 ? '+' : ''}${x.toFixed(1)}` : '—').padStart(6)
    console.log(`The level: ${target} LUFS integrated, true peak at most ${LEVEL.peak} dBTP. Clips in ${store.dir} not at it: ${queue.length}${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (groups.length) {
      console.log(`\n${'voice'.padEnd(22)} clips  LUFS now (p10 … p90)       gain (min … max)        kept  limited (over by)  filtered too  paced too`)
      for (const g of groups) {
        const lim = g.limited ? `${g.limited} (${g.over.toFixed(1)} dB)` : '0'
        console.log(`${g.name.padEnd(22)} ${String(g.clips).padStart(5)}  ${f1(g.lufs.median)} (${f1(g.lufs.p10)} … ${f1(g.lufs.p90)})  ${f1(g.gain.median)} (${f1(g.gain.min)} … ${f1(g.gain.max)})  ${String(g.kept).padStart(5)}  ${lim.padStart(17)}  ${String(g.denoise).padStart(12)}  ${String(g.paced).padStart(9)}`)
      }
      console.log(`(limited: the clips whose true peak the gain would take over ${LEVEL.peak - LIMIT_MARGIN} dB, where the limiter holds it, and by how much, the median)`)
      const unmeasured = rows.filter(r => !r.before).length
      if (unmeasured) console.log(`(${unmeasured} clip(s) not measured: no file, or ffmpeg failed)`)
    }
    if (!queue.length) process.exit(0)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each clip would get the gain (about 0.4 dB more where it is encoded again: the MP3 encode takes that off),`)
    console.log(`the limiter where its true peak would pass ${LEVEL.peak} dBTP, its voice's filter and a local clip's pace where they are due, in one encode; a clip within ${LEVEL.tolerance} dB`)
    console.log(`of the target keeps its file. The others are stored under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded.`)
    console.log(`Level with: companion/bin/voice-build --level --run${tail}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegLeveller()) {
    console.error('voice-build --level: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Levelling ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s) to ${target} LUFS …`)
  const r = await store.levelClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nLevelled ${r.done} clip(s) (${r.kept} kept as they were, ${r.limited} limited)${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done > r.kept) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (edges) {
  // the silence at every clip's edges: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const queue = store.edgesQueue()
  const tail = `${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  const what = `${EDGES.lead} s kept before the sound, ${EDGES.tail} s after it (sound: over ${EDGES.threshold} dBFS in 20 ms, back and on while over ${EDGES.floor})`
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    // each clip measured as its file is (they are at the level): nothing is written
    const measure = ffmpegFileEdges()
    if (!measure) console.error('voice-build --edges: no ffmpeg here (LANI_FFMPEG names one): nothing measured')
    const list = queue.slice(0, max)
    if (measure && list.length) console.error(`Measuring ${list.length} clip(s) …`)
    type Row = { key: string; voice: string; engine: string; method?: string | null; text: string; edges?: Edges; trim?: boolean }
    const rows: Row[] = []
    let next = 0
    await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 8 }, async () => {
      while (next < list.length) {
        const c = list[next++]
        const path = join(store.filesDir, c.file)
        const e = measure && FILE.test(c.file) && existsSync(path) ? await measure(path) : null
        rows.push({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, engine: c.engine, method: c.method ?? null, text: c.text, ...(e ? { edges: e, trim: trimmable(e, true) } : {}) })
      }
    }))
    const q = (xs: number[], f: number) => {
      const v = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b)
      return v.length ? v[Math.min(v.length - 1, Math.floor(f * (v.length - 1) + 0.5))] : NaN
    }
    // after: a trimmed clip's silence down to EDGES; the others' as it is
    const after = (r: Row) => (r.trim ? { lead: Math.min(r.edges!.lead, EDGES.lead), tail: Math.min(r.edges!.tail, EDGES.tail) } : r.edges!)
    const groupOf = (r: Row) => `${r.engine}${r.method === 'carrier' ? ' carrier' : ''}`
    const by = new Map<string, Row[]>()
    for (const r of rows) by.set(groupOf(r), [...(by.get(groupOf(r)) ?? []), r])
    const group = (name: string, g: Row[]) => {
      const m = g.filter(r => r.edges)
      const st = (xs: number[]) => ({ median: q(xs, 0.5), p90: q(xs, 0.9) })
      return {
        name, clips: g.length, measured: m.length, trim: m.filter(r => r.trim).length,
        lead: { now: st(m.map(r => r.edges!.lead)), after: st(m.map(r => after(r).lead)) },
        tail: { now: st(m.map(r => r.edges!.tail)), after: st(m.map(r => after(r).tail)) },
        seconds: m.reduce((n, r) => n + r.edges!.lead - after(r).lead + r.edges!.tail - after(r).tail, 0),
      }
    }
    const groups = [...[...by].map(([n, g]) => group(n, g)).sort((a, b) => b.clips - a.clips), ...(by.size > 1 ? [group('all', rows)] : [])]
    const summary = { edges: EDGES, waiting: queue.length, measured: rows.filter(r => r.edges).length, trim: rows.filter(r => r.trim).length, ffmpeg: !!measure, dir: store.dir }
    if (flag('--json')) {
      // and how many have more than 0.15 s at either edge (October 2026's measure)
      const over = (g: Row[]) => g.filter(r => r.edges && (r.edges.lead > 0.15 || r.edges.tail > 0.15)).length
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, over_015: Object.fromEntries([...by].map(([n, g]) => [n, over(g)])), groups: Object.fromEntries(groups.map(({ name, ...g }) => [name, g])), clips: rows }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    const f2 = (x: number) => (Number.isFinite(x) ? x.toFixed(2) : '—')
    console.log(`The edges: ${what}.`)
    console.log(`Clips in ${store.dir} not through it yet: ${queue.length}${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (groups.length && measure) {
      console.log(`\n${'engine'.padEnd(20)} clips   to trim  before: now (p90) → after     after: now (p90) → after    trimmed`)
      for (const g of groups) {
        console.log(`${g.name.padEnd(20)} ${String(g.clips).padStart(5)}  ${String(g.trim).padStart(10)}  ${`${f2(g.lead.now.median)} (${f2(g.lead.now.p90)}) → ${f2(g.lead.after.median)} (${f2(g.lead.after.p90)})`.padEnd(26)}  ${`${f2(g.tail.now.median)} (${f2(g.tail.now.p90)}) → ${f2(g.tail.after.median)} (${f2(g.tail.after.p90)})`.padEnd(26)} ${(g.seconds / 60).toFixed(1)} min`)
      }
      console.log(`(before / after: the silence before and after the sound, seconds, the median and p90; to trim: the clips with more than ${EDGES.slack.lead} s before it or ${EDGES.slack.tail} s after it)`)
      const unmeasured = rows.filter(r => !r.edges).length
      if (unmeasured) console.log(`(${unmeasured} clip(s) not measured: no file, or ffmpeg failed)`)
    }
    if (!queue.length) process.exit(0)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. The clips to trim are trimmed and brought to the level again in one encode, each under a new`)
    console.log('file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded; the others are only recorded. No engine is asked, no characters spent.')
    console.log(`Trim with: companion/bin/voice-build --edges --run${tail}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegLeveller()) {
    console.error('voice-build --edges: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Through the edges: ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s): ${what} …`)
  const r = await store.edgesClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\n${r.done} clip(s) done: ${r.trimmed} trimmed, ${r.kept} kept as they were${r.limited ? `, ${r.limited} limited` : ''}${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done > r.kept) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (restore) {
  // the local clips paced before, back from a snapshot: no engine, no ffmpeg
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const run = flag('--run')
  const quiet = flag('--json')
  console.error(`The local clips paced before (tempo set) in ${store.dir}, from ${snapshot} …`)
  const r = store.restorePaced(snapshot!, { run, max, out: quiet ? undefined : line => console.log(line) })
  if (quiet) console.log(JSON.stringify(r, null, 2))
  else {
    console.log(`\nPaced local clips: ${r.paced}. ${run ? 'Restored' : 'To restore'}: ${r.restored}${run ? ` (${r.verified} byte for byte the snapshot's file)` : ''}; not restorable: ${r.missing.length}${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} changed meanwhile` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; still paced: ${r.left}.`)
    if (!run && r.restored) console.log(`Dry run: nothing changed. Restore with: companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard ${snapshotArg} --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    if (run && r.restored) console.log('Then trim their edges: companion/bin/voice-build --edges --run. A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated).')
  }
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (tempo) {
  // the pace (a voice's own tempo, the local voice's pace): ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const set = store.pace
  const voices = tempoVoices()
  // "girl (elevenlabs ×1.1)"
  const own = Object.entries(voices).map(([v, t]) => `${v} (${typeof t === 'number' ? `×${t}` : Object.entries(t).map(([e, f]) => `${e} ×${f}`).join(', ')})`)
  const queue = store.tempoQueue()
  if (!set) {
    const st = store.tempoStats()
    // nothing at all to do: no pace, no voice's tempo, no clip paced at a tempo its voice no longer has
    const nothing = !own.length && !queue.length
    // (with --json on stderr: stdout is the JSON)
    const note = flag('--json') && !nothing ? console.error : console.log
    note(`The local voice keeps its own pace (no LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_TEMPO or LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_PAUSES)${own.length ? '.' : `, and no voice has a tempo of its own (the cast's "tempo")${nothing ? ': nothing to pace.' : '.'}`}`)
    if (st.paced) note(`${st.paced} local clip(s) were paced before: back with companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard <a snapshot from before>, then --edges.`)
    note('Their silence at the edges is trimmed as every clip\'s: companion/bin/voice-build --edges.')
    if (nothing) process.exit(0)
  }
  const factor = set?.tempo ?? null
  const chars = queue.reduce((n, c) => n + c.text.trim().length, 0)
  const tail = `${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  const local = set ? `the local voice's ${set.pause ? `pauses over ${set.pause} s down to it (LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_PAUSES), ` : ''}${set.tempo !== 1 ? `sped up ×${set.tempo} (LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_TEMPO), the pitch kept, ` : ''}the edges trimmed` : ''
  const what = [own.length ? `the voices' own tempo (the cast's "tempo"): ${own.join(', ')}, the pitch kept` : '', local].filter(Boolean).join('; ')
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    const pace = ffmpegPace()
    if (!pace) console.error(`voice-build ${paceFlag}: no ffmpeg here (LANI_FFMPEG names one): nothing measured`)
    const list = queue.slice(0, max)
    // characters a second on texts of 15 to 80 characters (a lone word is mostly its edges)
    const sentence = (t: string) => t.trim().length >= 15 && t.trim().length <= 80
    const q = (xs: number[], f: number) => {
      const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b)
      return s.length ? s[Math.min(s.length - 1, Math.floor(f * (s.length - 1) + 0.5))] : NaN
    }
    const stat = (xs: number[]) => ({ median: q(xs, 0.5), p10: q(xs, 0.1), p90: q(xs, 0.9), n: xs.length })
    // [n] clips spread over [all] (the same ones every time)
    const spread = <T,>(all: T[], n: number) => (all.length <= n ? all : Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => all[Math.floor((i * all.length) / n)]))
    const measureAll = async <T extends { file: string },>(xs: T[], af: (x: T) => string | undefined) => {
      const out: (T & { pace?: Pace; after?: Pace })[] = []
      let next = 0
      await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 4 }, async () => {
        while (next < xs.length) {
          const x = xs[next++]
          const path = join(store.filesDir, x.file)
          const bytes = pace && FILE.test(x.file) && existsSync(path) ? new Uint8Array(readFileSync(path)) : undefined
          const now = bytes ? await pace!(bytes) : null
          const chain = af(x)
          const after = bytes && chain ? await pace!(bytes, chain) : null
          out.push({ ...x, ...(now ? { pace: now } : {}), ...(after ? { after } : {}) })
        }
      }))
      return out
    }
    if (list.length && pace) console.error(`Measuring ${list.length} clip(s) …`)
    // each clip as it is now and as it would be paced: from the factor it is at to the one it waits for (paceDue)
    const rows = (await measureAll(list, c => { const d = store.paceDue(c); return d ? paceChain(d) || undefined : undefined })).map(r => ({ ...r, to: store.paceDue(r) }))
    // the reference: ElevenLabs' clips of the local clips' voices; and the local clips paced already, as they are now
    const localVoices = [...new Set(store.database.query("SELECT DISTINCT voice FROM clips WHERE engine = 'gepard'").all().map(r => (r as { voice: string }).voice))]
    const ofVoices = (engine: string) => (store.database.query(`SELECT * FROM clips WHERE engine = ? AND voice IN (${localVoices.map(() => '?').join(', ') || "''"}) ORDER BY key`).all(engine, ...localVoices) as Clip[]).filter(c => sentence(c.text))
    const eleven = pace && set ? await measureAll(spread(ofVoices('elevenlabs'), 120), () => undefined) : []
    const done = pace && set ? await measureAll(spread(ofVoices('gepard').filter(c => c.tempo === factor), 120), () => undefined) : []
    const rate = (xs: { text: string; pace?: Pace }[], k: 'pace' | 'after' = 'pace') =>
      stat(xs.filter(x => sentence(x.text) && (x as Record<string, unknown>)[k]).map(x => charsPerSecond(x.text, ((x as Record<string, unknown>)[k] as Pace).secs)))
    const by = new Map<string, typeof rows>()
    for (const r of rows) by.set(`${r.voice} ${r.engine}`, [...(by.get(`${r.voice} ${r.engine}`) ?? []), r])
    const group = (name: string, g: typeof rows) => {
      const m = g.filter(r => r.pace && r.after)
      const sum = (k: 'pace' | 'after') => m.reduce((n, r) => n + r[k]!.secs, 0)
      return {
        name, clips: g.length, measured: m.length, by: [...new Set(g.map(r => r.to?.tempo))].filter(t => t !== undefined),
        rate: { now: rate(m), after: rate(m, 'after') },
        edges: { now: stat(m.map(r => r.pace!.lead + r.pace!.tail)).median, after: stat(m.map(r => r.after!.lead + r.after!.tail)).median },
        paused: { now: stat(m.map(r => r.pace!.paused)).median, after: stat(m.map(r => r.after!.paused)).median },
        seconds: { now: sum('pace'), after: sum('after') },
      }
    }
    const groups = [...[...by].map(([v, g]) => group(v, g)).sort((a, b) => b.clips - a.clips), ...(by.size > 1 ? [group('all', rows)] : [])]
    const summary = { tempo: factor, pace: set, voices, waiting: queue.length, chars, measured: rows.filter(r => r.after).length, ffmpeg: !!pace, dir: store.dir, elevenlabs: rate(eleven), paced: rate(done) }
    if (flag('--json')) {
      // voices: each voice's clips (by engine) as they are and as they would be paced; cast: the voices' own tempos
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, voices: Object.fromEntries(groups.map(({ name, ...g }) => [name, g])), cast: voices, clips: rows.map(({ key, voice, engine, file, text, tempo, to, pace, after }) => ({ key, voice, engine, file, text, tempo, by: to?.tempo, now: pace, after })) }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    const f1 = (x: number, w = 5) => (Number.isFinite(x) ? x.toFixed(1) : '—').padStart(w)
    const r3 = (s: { median: number; p10: number; p90: number }) => `${f1(s.median)} (${f1(s.p10, 4)} … ${f1(s.p90, 4)})`
    console.log(`The pace: ${what || 'none'}.`)
    console.log(`Clips in ${store.dir} not at their pace: ${queue.length} (${chars} characters)${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (groups.length && pace) {
      console.log(`\n${'voice'.padEnd(22)} clips  by      chars/s now (p10 … p90)   paced (p10 … p90)     edges now → paced   pauses now → paced   length now → paced`)
      for (const g of groups) {
        const edges = `${g.edges.now.toFixed(2)} → ${g.edges.after.toFixed(2)} s`
        const pauses = `${g.paused.now.toFixed(2)} → ${g.paused.after.toFixed(2)} s`
        const by = g.by.length === 1 ? `×${g.by[0]}` : g.by.length ? 'mixed' : ''
        console.log(`${g.name.padEnd(22)} ${String(g.clips).padStart(5)}  ${by.padEnd(6)}  ${r3(g.rate.now)}    ${r3(g.rate.after)}  ${edges.padStart(17)}   ${pauses.padStart(18)}   ${(g.seconds.now / 60).toFixed(1)} → ${(g.seconds.after / 60).toFixed(1)} min`)
      }
      console.log('(chars/s: the medians of texts of 15 to 80 characters; by: the factor from the clip as it is; edges: the silence before and after the sound, pauses: of 0.1 s or more in all; the medians a clip)')
      const unmeasured = rows.filter(r => !r.after).length
      if (unmeasured) console.log(`(${unmeasured} clip(s) not measured: no file, or ffmpeg failed)`)
    }
    if (pace && summary.elevenlabs.n) console.log(`\nElevenLabs, the same voices (${summary.elevenlabs.n} clips of 15 to 80 characters): ${r3(summary.elevenlabs)} chars/s`)
    if (pace && summary.paced.n) console.log(`Local clips paced already (×${factor}; ${summary.paced.n} of 15 to 80 characters): ${r3(summary.paced)} chars/s`)
    if (!queue.length) process.exit(0)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each clip would be paced and brought to the level again in one encode, under a new file name, the`)
    console.log('old file removed once the new one is recorded. No engine is asked, no characters spent.')
    console.log(`Pace with: companion/bin/voice-build ${paceFlag} --run${tail}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegLeveller()) {
    console.error(`voice-build ${paceFlag}: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)`)
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Pacing ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s): ${what} …`)
  const r = await store.tempoClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nPaced ${r.done} clip(s)${r.limited ? ` (${r.limited} limited)` : ''}${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
const packs =new PackStore(packsDirs(process.env.LANI_PACKS_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/packs'), cultures, culture, language), join(appDir, 'packs'))
const modules = new ModuleStore(join(appDir, 'modules'), ofLanguage(process.env.LANI_MODULES_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/modules')), log)
const scenarios = new ScenarioStore(ofLanguage(process.env.LANI_SCENARIOS_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/scenarios')), join(appDir, 'scenarios'))
const villagers = new VillagerStore(process.env.LANI_VILLAGERS_DIR ?? join(cultureDir(cultures, culture), 'villagers'), join(appDir, 'villagers'), log)
const scenes = new SceneStore(scenesDirs(process.env.LANI_SCENES_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/scenes'), cultures, culture, language), join(appDir, 'scenes'), () => ({ packs: packs.all(), scenarios: scenarios.all(), villagers: villagers.all() }), log)
// the storyteller's stories: the village's culture pack's (its stories/), and the tutor's, as the bridge has them
const stories = new StoryStore(storiesDirs(cultures, culture), join(appDir, 'stories'), () => ({ packs: packs.all(), villagers: villagers.all() }), log)
// the car's audio drills of the village's language (companion/drills/<language>), as the bridge has them
const drills = new DrillStore(drillsDir(process.env.LANI_DRILLS_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/drills'), language), language, () => ({ packs: packs.all(), villagers: villagers.all() }), log)
// the grammar book of the village's language and the tutor's pages: their examples, as the bridge has them
const grammar = new GrammarStore(grammarDir(process.env.LANI_GRAMMAR_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/grammar'), language), language, join(appDir, 'grammar'), log)
// the school's course of the village's language (companion/course/<language>), as the bridge serves it (GET /course): its
// exercises' texts per base in the learner's own language (the profile's)
const course = new CourseStore(courseDir(process.env.LANI_COURSE_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/course'), language), language, join(appDir, 'course'), log, () => learnerLangs(dirname(appDir), language).base)
// how the cast are introduced as they arrive: the culture pack's (arrivals.json), the tutor's for one of them replacing it
const arrivals = (() => {
  const byId = new Map(Object.entries(cultureArrivals(cultures, culture, language).file?.cast ?? {}).map(([id, a]) => [id, { id, levels: a.levels }]))
  for (const a of new ArrivalStore(join(appDir, 'arrivals'), log).all()) if (a.language === language) byId.set(a.id, { id: a.id, levels: a.levels })
  return [...byId.values()]
})()

const { eleven, gepard } = enginesFromEnv(process.env, log, language)
// the local worker speaks only Slovene; a culture's cast without voices yet voices nothing (the phone's TTS speaks)
const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: language === 'sl' ? [eleven, gepard] : castVoiced() ? [eleven] : [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
// the voices of their own that are ready (the voice profiles, in the store's database): a storyteller who has one tells
// in it ("@janez", as the app asks for it by the fire), and ElevenLabs makes those clips in it
const own = ownVoicesIn(store.database)
usePersonVoices(id => own.get(id))
const noVoice = only.filter(s => PERSON_VOICE.test(s) && !personVoice(s))
if (noVoice.length) {
  console.error(`--only: no voice of their own (yet): ${noVoice.join(', ')}`)
  process.exit(2)
}

if (toEleven) {
  // a speaker's local (Gepard) clips again in their ElevenLabs voice: the store and ElevenLabs, no corpus
  const now = eleven.model
  const queue = store.localQueue(elevenSpeakers)
  const q = await eleven.subscription()
  const reserve = eleven.reserve
  const room = q ? Math.max(0, q.limit - q.used - reserve) : 0
  const budget = maxChars !== undefined ? Math.min(room, maxChars) : room
  const cost = (c: Clip) => eleven.cost(c.text, c.voice, explanationLang(c.norm))
  const would: Clip[] = []
  let spend = 0
  for (const c of queue) {
    if (max !== undefined && would.length >= max) break
    if (spend + cost(c) > budget) continue
    would.push(c)
    spend += cost(c)
  }
  const all = queue.reduce((n, c) => n + cost(c), 0)
  const n = (x: number) => x.toLocaleString('en-US')
  const summary = {
    speakers: elevenSpeakers, model: now, local: queue.length, local_chars: all, played: queue.filter(c => (c.hits ?? 0) > 0).length,
    quota: q ? { limit: q.limit, used: q.used, remaining: Math.max(0, q.limit - q.used), reserve, resets_at: q.resets_at } : null,
    would: { clips: would.length, chars: spend, credits: creditsFor(spend, now) }, dir: store.dir,
  }
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, clips: would.map(c => ({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, hits: c.hits ?? 0, chars: cost(c), source: c.source, text: c.text })) }, null, 2))
    else {
      console.log(`Local (Gepard) clips of ${elevenSpeakers.join(', ')} in ${store.dir}: ${n(queue.length)} (${n(all)} characters; ${n(summary.played)} played at least once)`)
      console.log(q ? `ElevenLabs: ${n(Math.max(0, q.limit - q.used))} of ${n(q.limit)} characters left, ${n(reserve)} kept for live lines${q.resets_at ? `, resets ${new Date(q.resets_at * 1000).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}` : ''}` : 'ElevenLabs: not available (no ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, or the subscription could not be read)')
      console.log(`--run would make ${n(would.length)} in their ElevenLabs voice (${n(spend)} characters, ≈ ${n(creditsFor(spend, now))} credits with ${now}), most played first:`)
      for (const c of would.slice(0, 15)) console.log(`  ${String(c.hits ?? 0).padStart(4)}× ${c.voice.padEnd(11)} ${(c.source ?? '').padEnd(24)} ${c.text.length > 50 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 49)}…` : c.text}`)
      if (would.length > 15) console.log(`  … and ${n(would.length - 15)} more`)
      console.log('\nDry run: nothing changed. Each would be made in its ElevenLabs voice, filtered, trimmed and levelled as every new clip,')
      console.log('under a new file name, the local file removed; a running bridge tells the app.')
      console.log(`Make them with: companion/bin/voice-build --elevenlabs ${elevenSpeakers.join(',')} --run${maxChars !== undefined ? ` --max-chars ${maxChars}` : ''}${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    }
    process.exit(0)
  }
  console.log(`Making ${n(would.length)} of ${n(queue.length)} local clip(s) in their ElevenLabs voice with ${now} (${n(spend)} characters at most) …`)
  const r = await store.elevenlabsFor(elevenSpeakers, { max, maxChars: budget, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nMade ${n(r.made)} in ElevenLabs (${n(r.chars)} characters, ≈ ${n(creditsFor(r.chars, now))} credits)${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no ElevenLabs voice for them now)` : ''}; ${n(r.left)} left${r.stopped ? ` (stopped: ${r.stopped})` : ''}.`)
  if (r.made) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.stopped && !r.made ? 1 : 0)
}

if (toDrama3) {
  // a speaker's local Gepard clips again with Drama 3, on the worker started for the batch: the store, no corpus
  if (language !== 'sl') {
    console.error(`voice-build --drama3: the Drama 3 voices speak Slovene (companion/voice-drama3/voices.json); this village speaks ${language}`)
    process.exit(2)
  }
  const s = drama3Settings(process.env)
  const d3 = new Drama3({ url: s.url, log })
  const retry = flag('--retry-failed')
  const queue = store.drama3Queue(d3Speakers, retry)
  const failedBefore = store.drama3Failed(d3Speakers)
  const would = max !== undefined ? queue.slice(0, max) : queue
  const est = drama3Estimate(would.map(c => c.text), s.rtf)
  const n = (x: number) => x.toLocaleString('en-US')
  const by: Record<string, { clips: number; audio: number }> = {}
  for (const c of queue) {
    const b = (by[c.voice] ??= { clips: 0, audio: 0 })
    b.clips++
    b.audio += drama3Estimate([c.text], s.rtf).audio
  }
  const health = await d3.health()
  const mem = availableGb(s.meminfo)
  const summary = {
    speakers: d3Speakers, local: queue.length, played: queue.filter(c => (c.hits ?? 0) > 0).length, chars: queue.reduce((k, c) => k + c.text.length, 0),
    by_voice: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(by).map(([v, b]) => [v, { clips: b.clips, audio_seconds: Math.round(b.audio) }])),
    would: { clips: would.length, audio_seconds: Math.round(est.audio), seconds: Math.round(est.seconds) },
    rtf: s.rtf, failed_before: failedBefore.length, retry_failed: retry,
    worker: { url: s.url, up: health?.ok === true, waiting: health && health.ok !== true ? (health.waiting ?? health.error ?? null) : null, cmd: s.cmd.join(' '), installed: s.installed, log: s.log },
    memory: { available_gb: mem === undefined ? null : Math.round(mem * 10) / 10, min_free_gb: s.minFreeGb }, lock: s.lock, dir: store.dir,
  }
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, failed: failedBefore, clips: would.map(c => ({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, hits: c.hits ?? 0, source: c.source, text: c.text })) }, null, 2))
    else {
      console.log(`Local (Gepard) clips of ${d3Speakers.join(', ')} in ${store.dir} for Drama 3: ${n(queue.length)} (${n(summary.chars)} characters, ≈ ${duration(Object.values(by).reduce((a, b) => a + b.audio, 0))} of audio; ${n(summary.played)} played at least once)`)
      for (const [v, b] of Object.entries(by).sort((a, b2) => b2[1].clips - a[1].clips)) console.log(`  ${v.padEnd(12)} ${String(b.clips).padStart(6)} clips  ≈ ${duration(b.audio)} of audio`)
      if (failedBefore.length) console.log(`${n(failedBefore.length)} line(s) no take passed before keep their Gepard clip${retry ? ': tried again (--retry-failed)' : ' (--retry-failed tries them again)'}.`)
      console.log(`--run would make ${n(would.length)} with Drama 3, most played first: ≈ ${duration(est.audio)} of audio in ≈ ${duration(est.seconds)} (${s.rtf} s a second of audio with the checks and retries, LANI_DRAMA3_RTF).`)
      for (const c of would.slice(0, 15)) console.log(`  ${String(c.hits ?? 0).padStart(4)}× ${c.voice.padEnd(11)} ${(c.source ?? '').padEnd(24)} ${c.text.length > 50 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 49)}…` : c.text}`)
      if (would.length > 15) console.log(`  … and ${n(would.length - 15)} more`)
      console.log(`The worker: ${summary.worker.up ? `up at ${s.url} (used as it is, not stopped after)` : health ? `at ${s.url}, waiting for ${String(summary.worker.waiting)}` : `not running; --run starts ${s.cmd.join(' ')}${s.installed ? '' : ' (NOT INSTALLED: companion/voice-drama3/install.sh)'} and stops it after`}.`)
      console.log(`It holds the heavy lock ${s.lock} while it runs (LANI_HEAVY_LOCK). Memory: ${mem === undefined ? '?' : mem.toFixed(1)} GB available now; the batch pauses below ${s.minFreeGb} GB.`)
      console.log('\nDry run: nothing changed. Each take passes the worker\'s checks (the gender by pitch, noise, the text heard by Whisper, length')
      console.log('and silence) or is made again; a line that never passes keeps its Gepard clip. Trimmed and levelled as every new clip,')
      console.log('under a new file name, the Gepard file removed; a running bridge tells the app. Built with Fish Audio.')
      console.log(`Make them with: companion/bin/voice-build --drama3 ${d3Arg} --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${retry ? ' --retry-failed' : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    }
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!would.length) {
    console.log(`Nothing to make: no local (Gepard) clips of ${d3Speakers.join(', ')} left for Drama 3${failedBefore.length ? ` (${failedBefore.length} failed before: --retry-failed)` : ''}.`)
    store.close()
    process.exit(0)
  }
  // Ctrl-C (or SIGTERM): the clips in flight are finished, then the worker stops; a second one stops at once
  let stopping = false
  let now = false
  const worker = new Drama3Worker(d3, s, line => console.log(line))
  const onSignal = () => {
    if (stopping) {
      now = true
      void worker.stop().finally(() => process.exit(130))
      return
    }
    stopping = true
    console.log('\nStopping after the clips in flight (again to stop at once); the next --run goes on from here.')
  }
  process.on('SIGINT', onSignal)
  process.on('SIGTERM', onSignal)
  console.log(`Making ${n(would.length)} of ${n(queue.length)} local clip(s) with Drama 3 (≈ ${duration(est.seconds)}) …`)
  const gate = memoryGate(worker, s, () => stopping, line => console.log(line))
  let r: Awaited<ReturnType<VoiceStore['drama3For']>> | undefined
  let error: string | undefined
  try {
    if (!(await gate())) throw new Error('stopped')
    await worker.start()
    const t0 = Date.now()
    r = await store.drama3For(d3, d3Speakers, { max, retry, concurrency: 2, before: gate, out: line => console.log(line) })
    console.log(`\nMade ${n(r.made)} with Drama 3 in ${duration((Date.now() - t0) / 1000)}${r.failed ? `; ${n(r.failed)} failed every take (their Gepard clip stays: voice-build --drama3 ${d3Arg} --retry-failed tries them again)` : ''}${r.changed ? `; ${r.changed} changed meanwhile, left as they are` : ''}; ${n(r.left)} left${r.stopped ? ` (stopped: ${r.stopped})` : ''}.`)
  } catch (e) {
    error = (e as Error).message
  } finally {
    await worker.stop()
  }
  // stopped at once (a second Ctrl-C): the signal's handler ends the process
  if (now) await new Promise(() => {})
  if (error) console.error(`voice-build --drama3: ${error}`)
  const failedNow = store.drama3Failed(d3Speakers)
  if (failedNow.length) {
    console.log(`\nLines no take passed (${failedNow.length}; their Gepard clip stays):`)
    for (const f of failedNow.slice(-20)) console.log(`  ${f.voice.padEnd(11)} ${f.text.length > 50 ? `${f.text.slice(0, 49)}…` : f.text}  — ${f.reasons.at(-1) ?? ''}`)
  }
  if (r?.made) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...(r ?? {}), ...(error ? { error } : {}), failed_lines: failedNow }))
  store.close()
  process.exit(error || (r?.stopped && !r.made) ? 1 : 0)
}

if (upgradeModel) {
  // the ElevenLabs clips of an older model again in the current one: the store and ElevenLabs, no corpus
  const now = eleven.model
  const queue = store.modelQueue()
  const q = await eleven.subscription()
  const reserve = eleven.reserve
  const room = q ? Math.max(0, q.limit - q.used - reserve) : 0
  const budget = maxChars !== undefined ? Math.min(room, maxChars) : room
  const cost = (c: Clip) => eleven.cost(c.text, c.voice, explanationLang(c.norm))
  // what --run would make now, most played first, within the budget and --max
  const would: Clip[] = []
  let spend = 0
  for (const c of queue) {
    if (max !== undefined && would.length >= max) break
    if (spend + cost(c) > budget) continue
    would.push(c)
    spend += cost(c)
  }
  const by = store.modelStats()
  const from: Record<string, { clips: number; chars: number }> = {}
  for (const c of queue) {
    const m = modelOf(c)!
    const o = (from[m] ??= { clips: 0, chars: 0 })
    o.clips++
    o.chars += cost(c)
  }
  const summary = {
    model: now, by_model: by, older: queue.length, older_chars: queue.reduce((n, c) => n + cost(c), 0), from,
    played: queue.filter(c => (c.hits ?? 0) > 0).length,
    quota: q ? { limit: q.limit, used: q.used, remaining: Math.max(0, q.limit - q.used), reserve, resets_at: q.resets_at } : null,
    would: { clips: would.length, chars: spend, credits: creditsFor(spend, now) }, dir: store.dir,
  }
  const n = (x: number) => x.toLocaleString('en-US')
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, clips: would.map(c => ({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, model: modelOf(c), hits: c.hits ?? 0, chars: cost(c), text: c.text })) }, null, 2))
    else {
      console.log(`ElevenLabs clips in ${store.dir} by model: ${Object.entries(by).map(([m, x]) => `${m} ${n(x.clips)} (${n(x.chars)} chars)`).join(', ') || 'none'}`)
      console.log(`New clips are made with ${now} (LANI_ELEVENLABS_MODEL). Made with an older model: ${n(queue.length)} (${n(summary.older_chars)} characters to send; ${n(summary.played)} played at least once)` +
        `${Object.keys(from).length ? `: ${Object.entries(from).map(([m, x]) => `${m} ${n(x.clips)}`).join(', ')}` : ''}`)
      console.log(q ? `ElevenLabs: ${n(Math.max(0, q.limit - q.used))} of ${n(q.limit)} characters left, ${n(reserve)} kept for live lines${q.resets_at ? `, resets ${new Date(q.resets_at * 1000).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}` : ''}` : 'ElevenLabs: not available (no ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, or the subscription could not be read)')
      console.log(`--run would make ${n(would.length)} again (${n(spend)} characters, ≈ ${n(creditsFor(spend, now))} credits with ${now}), most played first:`)
      for (const c of would.slice(0, 15)) console.log(`  ${String(c.hits ?? 0).padStart(4)}× ${modelOf(c)!.padEnd(16)} ${c.voice.padEnd(11)} ${c.text.length > 60 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 59)}…` : c.text}`)
      if (would.length > 15) console.log(`  … and ${n(would.length - 15)} more`)
      console.log('\nDry run: nothing changed. Each would be made again in its voice, filtered, trimmed and levelled as every new clip, under')
      console.log('a new file name, the old file removed; a running bridge tells the app. Local (Gepard) clips and family recordings stay.')
      console.log(`Upgrade with: companion/bin/voice-build --upgrade-model --run${maxChars !== undefined ? ` --max-chars ${maxChars}` : ' --max-chars N'}${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    }
    process.exit(0)
  }
  console.log(`Making ${n(would.length)} of ${n(queue.length)} clip(s) again with ${now} (${n(spend)} characters at most) …`)
  const r = await store.upgradeModel({ max, maxChars: budget, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nMade ${n(r.made)} again with ${now} (${n(r.chars)} characters, ≈ ${n(creditsFor(r.chars, now))} credits)${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no ElevenLabs voice for them now)` : ''}; ${n(r.left)} left${r.stopped ? ` (stopped: ${r.stopped})` : ''}.`)
  if (r.made) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.stopped && !r.made ? 1 : 0)
}
// the app's check for the language learned (Speaker.isSlovene) besides how a text reads: a clip of it on the node in any
// voice (its /voice/index), or a family recording of it
const clipIndex = store.index()
const familyIndex = (() => {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(appDir, 'audio', 'index.json'), 'utf8')) as Record<string, unknown[]>
  } catch {
    return {}
  }
})()
// the learner's own languages the course's explanations are read in: --base, else the learner profile's
const courseBases = bases.length ? bases : [learnerLangs(dirname(appDir), language).base]
const everything = corpus({
  packs: packs.all(),
  modules: modules.list().filter(m => !m.tags.includes('retired')).flatMap(m => modules.get(m.id) ?? []),
  scenarios: scenarios.all(),
  scenes: scenes.resolved(),
  // the culture's keepers' talks (world.json `spots`: the charcoal burner's meeting and his story, every telling)
  keepers: cultureKeepers(cultures, culture).map(k => ({ ...k, tellings: keeperTellings(k) })),
  // the village projects' steps as short scenes (project-steps/: every telling, each line in its speaker's voice)
  // and the ages' parties (celebrations/: every telling, each line in its speaker's voice), as a step's
  steps: [
    ...cultureStepFiles(cultures, culture).map(f => ({ project: f.project, tellings: stepTellings(f) })),
    ...cultureCelebrationFiles(cultures, culture).map(f => ({ project: `party:${f.age}`, tellings: partyTellings(f) })),
  ],
  villagers: villagers.all(),
  stories: stories.all(),
  drills: drills.all(),
  grammar: grammar.all(),
  // the school's course, read in the teacher's voice (the explanations in the learner's own language apart: --explanations)
  course: { units: course.served()?.units ?? [], pages: grammar.all(), bases: courseBases, has: t => indexHas(clipIndex, t) || familyHas(familyIndex, t) },
  arrivals,
  // «Vidim, vidim»: what a child says playing I spy in the scenes (companion/ispy, the app bundles it)
  ispy: readISpy(process.env.LANI_ISPY_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/ispy')),
  ownVoice: id => !!personVoice(`@${id}`),
  cards: (() => {
    const sr = join(appDir, '..', 'spaced-repetition.json')
    return existsSync(sr) ? cardTexts(JSON.parse(readFileSync(sr, 'utf8')).items ?? {}) : []
  })(),
  language,
  // rendered for the learner ({learner}, {m:…|f:…}: addressee.ts), as the app says it
  learner: addresseeOf(join(appDir, '..'), language),
  // the learner's own lines (the dialogs' choices) in their voice (my-voice.ts: their choice in learner-profile.json, else
  // the default of their gender and age; the child flag LANI_CHILD, else their registry entry's); none while it's off
  mine: mineVoice(join(appDir, '..'), addresseeOf(join(appDir, '..'), language), childOf(join(appDir, '..'), root)),
})
// --only: the texts of those voices (someone's own voice counts as their speaker's: "@mojca" as the teacher's)
const ofOnly = (v: string) => !only.length || only.includes(v) || (!!personVoice(v) && only.includes(personVoice(v)!.archetype))
// the course's explanations: in the plan and the run with --explanations, else counted apart
const items = everything.filter(i => ofOnly(i.voice) && (explanations || !i.lang))
const leftOut = explanations ? [] : everything.filter(i => ofOnly(i.voice) && !!i.lang)

if (narrators) {
  // the narrators' Slovene clips in their local voice: the corpus tells which are Slovene, no ElevenLabs
  if (!villageVoices.narrators) {
    console.log(`The narrators of this village (${language}) speak as its voice cast has them: nothing to do.`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  // Slovene: a clip of this village's corpus, of a source the corpus has, or a line the app spoke here
  const keys = new Set(items.map(i => clipKey(normalizeText(i.text), i.voice)))
  const sources = new Set(items.map(i => i.source))
  const spoken = new Set(['live', 'road'])
  const slovene = (c: Clip) => keys.has(c.key) || sources.has(c.source) || spoken.has(c.source)
  const { todo, skipped } = store.narratorQueue(slovene)
  // each clip's voice now, and the local voice it is made in (female: ana for a lone word, nina for a sentence)
  const count = (xs: Clip[]) => {
    const by: Record<string, number> = {}
    for (const c of xs) {
      const k = `${c.voice} ${c.engine}${c.method === 'carrier' ? ' carrier' : ''}${c.engine === 'gepard' ? ` (${c.engine_voice ?? (c.voice === 'female' ? 'ana' : '—')})` : ''} → ${store.localVoiceOf(c.voice, c.text)}`
      by[k] = (by[k] ?? 0) + 1
    }
    return by
  }
  const up = await gepard.up()
  const voices = { female: store.localVoiceOf('female', 'Dober dan, Jan.'), male: store.localVoiceOf('male', 'Dober dan, Jan.') }
  const words = { female: store.localVoiceOf('female', 'kosilo'), male: store.localVoiceOf('male', 'kosilo') }
  const named = (g: 'female' | 'male') => `${g} ${voices[g]}${words[g] !== voices[g] ? ` (a lone word: ${words[g]})` : ''}`
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) {
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ voices, words, todo: todo.length, chars: todo.reduce((n, c) => n + c.text.length, 0), by: count(todo), skipped: skipped.map(c => ({ key: c.key, source: c.source, engine: c.engine, text: c.text })), gepard_up: up, dir: store.dir }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    console.log(`The narrators' local voices: ${named('female')}, ${named('male')}. Their local clips in ${store.dir} not in them yet: ${todo.length + skipped.length}`)
    for (const [k, n] of Object.entries(count(todo)).sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])) console.log(`  ${k.padEnd(40)} ${String(n).padStart(5)}`)
    console.log(`Slovene, to make again: ${todo.length} (${todo.reduce((n, c) => n + c.text.length, 0)} characters; about ${Math.ceil(todo.length / 60)} minutes at a second a clip)${max !== undefined && max < todo.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (skipped.length) {
      console.log(`Left as they are, not known to be Slovene (not in this village's corpus, its sources, or spoken here): ${skipped.length}`)
      for (const c of skipped) console.log(`  · ${c.voice.padEnd(7)} ${c.source.padEnd(24)} ${c.text.length > 60 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 59)}…` : c.text}`)
    }
    console.log(`Local Gepard worker: ${up ? 'up' : 'down (the run needs it)'}`)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each is made again by the local worker, its edges trimmed and levelled, under a new file name, the old`)
    console.log('file removed once the new one is recorded. No ElevenLabs; the clips in the narrators\' Slovene ElevenLabs voices stay as they are.')
    console.log('The run can stop any time: the next one goes on where it stopped.')
    console.log(`Re-voice with: companion/bin/voice-build --narrators --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!up) {
    console.error('voice-build --narrators: the local Gepard worker is down (LANI_GEPARD_URL)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Re-voicing ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, todo.length) : todo.length} of ${todo.length} narrator clip(s) in the local voice (${named('female')}, ${named('male')}) …`)
  const r = await store.revoiceNarrators(slovene, { max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nMade ${r.made} again in the local voice${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} changed meanwhile` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} left${r.stopped ? ` (stopped: ${r.stopped})` : ''}.`)
  if (r.made) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed || r.stopped ? 1 : 0)
}

const opts = { maxChars, upgrade: flag('--upgrade'), revoice, revoiceWords, max, leftOut, ...(only.length ? { only } : {}) }

const before = await plan(items, store, eleven, gepard, opts)
if (flag('--json') && !flag('--run')) {
  console.log(JSON.stringify(before, null, 2))
  process.exit(0)
}
console.log(formatPlan(before, store.dir))
if (!flag('--run')) {
  const tail = `${only.length ? ` --only ${only.join(',')}` : ''}${explanations ? ' --explanations' : ''}${bases.length ? ` --base ${bases.join(',')}` : ''}${maxChars !== undefined ? ` --max-chars ${maxChars}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  console.log(`\nDry run. ${revoiceWords ? `Re-voice with: companion/bin/voice-build --revoice-words --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}` : `Generate with: companion/bin/voice-build --run${tail}`}`)
  process.exit(0)
}

if (revoiceWords) {
  // only the old-style short narrator words, in their carrier sentence; the corpus stays as it is
  console.log('\nRe-voicing short narrator words …')
  const r = await store.revoiceWords({ max, maxChars, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nRe-voiced ${r.made} word(s) in their carrier sentence (${r.chars} chars)${r.plain ? `; ${r.plain} kept plain (the word could not be cut out)` : ''}; ${r.left} old-style left.`)
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(0)
}

console.log('\nGenerating …')
const r = await run(items, store, { ...opts, out: line => console.log(line) })
console.log(`\nMade ${r.made.elevenlabs} ElevenLabs clip(s) (${r.chars} chars; ${r.replaced} replaced a clip) and ${r.made.gepard} local clip(s); ${r.left} left for later.`)
if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
store.close()
